WEBVTT

00:01.140 --> 00:04.730
<b>Tsubame West School Festival</b>

00:04.730 --> 00:07.360
<b>Tsubame West School Festival</b>

00:07.360 --> 00:09.500
The quiz battle starts at 10!

00:07.360 --> 00:10.440
<b>Fastest Fingers First!
Quiz</b>

00:09.500 --> 00:11.460
Visit our kimono cafe!

00:10.440 --> 00:12.670
Would you like some takoyaki?

00:12.670 --> 00:14.430
Come watch us!

00:14.430 --> 00:15.600
Take this flyer.

00:15.600 --> 00:17.440
We're about to start!

00:19.200 --> 00:21.200
<b>Guaranteed Tasty
\hTakoyaki</b>

00:19.200 --> 00:21.200
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:19.200 --> 00:21.200
<b>Crepes</b>

00:21.200 --> 00:23.710
We're distributing indoor slippers here!

00:23.710 --> 00:25.000
Here you go.

00:25.000 --> 00:26.830
<i>Day one of the school festival.</i>

00:26.830 --> 00:28.920
Good turnout this year, huh?

00:28.920 --> 00:31.640
Right? Well, we do have 
clear skies and warm weather.

00:31.640 --> 00:33.510
Seriously.

00:34.370 --> 00:36.370
<i>It's off to a great start!</i>

00:37.330 --> 00:40.710
<i>So dazzling</i>

00:40.710 --> 00:44.150
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

00:44.870 --> 00:47.770
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

00:47.770 --> 00:50.560
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

01:04.910 --> 01:07.630
<i>In such a narrow world</i>

01:07.630 --> 01:11.420
<i>Your vibrant laughter</i>

01:11.420 --> 01:14.380
<i>Resonates so beautifully</i>

01:14.380 --> 01:17.190
<i>And that's what saved me</i>

01:17.630 --> 01:21.290
<i>If we relive this moment</i>

01:21.290 --> 01:24.510
<i>In an unimaginable future</i>

01:24.510 --> 01:27.480
<i>Even if we're lost, it's okay</i>

01:27.480 --> 01:31.320
<i>We will be in it together</i>

01:32.010 --> 01:35.310
<i>So dazzling</i>

01:35.310 --> 01:39.110
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

01:39.480 --> 01:42.400
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

01:42.400 --> 01:45.230
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

01:45.230 --> 01:48.560
<i>I was entranced</i>

01:48.560 --> 01:52.670
<i>By your lively figure</i>

01:52.670 --> 01:55.820
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

01:55.820 --> 01:58.600
<i>Is love, then…</i>

01:59.330 --> 02:02.460
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

02:02.460 --> 02:05.240
<i>Is love, then...</i>

02:07.930 --> 02:10.400
I want to attend this high school!

02:10.400 --> 02:14.530
How much did you study to get in, 
Student Council President?

02:14.530 --> 02:17.270
That really differs from person to person.

02:17.270 --> 02:20.750
Some people need ten hours a day, 
others only need two.

02:20.750 --> 02:23.450
I always made time for breaks.

02:23.450 --> 02:27.360
I studied when I could focus, 
and rested when I needed to.

02:27.360 --> 02:29.220
The key is to find the right balance.

02:29.220 --> 02:31.340
You really seem to have it together.

02:31.340 --> 02:32.670
No, not at all.

02:33.020 --> 02:35.120
Is there anything else you're worried about?

02:35.120 --> 02:36.280
If you don't mind...

02:36.280 --> 02:39.530
Kazakami-san, don't you have 
the next shift at the orientation table?

02:39.530 --> 02:40.540
Oops, I forgot.

02:40.540 --> 02:41.850
Sorry, but I have to go.

02:41.850 --> 02:43.260
S-Sure.

02:43.260 --> 02:46.720
Were you going to stay there chatting 
if I hadn't said anything?

02:46.720 --> 02:48.780
Hey, she needed advice.

02:48.780 --> 02:51.060
We can't make visitors wait at the table!

02:51.060 --> 02:53.360
Thanks for reminding me.

02:53.360 --> 02:55.600
You'll barely make it in time 
if you don't run!

02:55.600 --> 02:56.980
That's fine by me.

02:58.700 --> 03:02.360
<i>Takamine-senpai's been steaming for ages.</i>

03:02.360 --> 03:06.600
<i>I think Kazakami-senpai is smart and capable,</i>

03:06.600 --> 03:13.130
<i>but Takamine-senpai's been organizing 
since her first-year. She's used to this.</i>

03:13.130 --> 03:19.240
<i>This event's such a big deal, some students 
risk their college chances to participate.</i>

03:19.240 --> 03:21.130
<i>Takamine-senpai...</i>

03:21.130 --> 03:25.270
<i>I'm sure she must want to be 
president now more than ever.</i>

03:27.050 --> 03:29.130
Iwakura-san, you can take a break now.

03:29.130 --> 03:30.390
Okay!

03:39.500 --> 03:45.740
<i>Blooming by the window, my little rose.</i>

03:45.740 --> 03:51.580
<i>Shining in the rays of dawn, 
soaking in the evening dew.</i>

03:51.580 --> 03:54.770
<i>Even past these glorious days,</i>

03:54.770 --> 03:59.300
<i>bound together for eternity,</i>

03:59.770 --> 04:03.300
<i>my little rose.</i>

03:59.780 --> 04:03.300
<i>your little rose.</i>

04:09.310 --> 04:12.820
Let's take part in the 
upcoming music festival!

04:12.820 --> 04:14.220
Woo!

04:12.820 --> 04:14.220
Yay!

04:14.800 --> 04:18.450
To be in love is not a sin, Lyra.

04:19.430 --> 04:22.150
But this is merely how I feel.

04:22.150 --> 04:26.220
Johan, you must decide 
how to live your own life.

04:27.780 --> 04:28.360
Hurry!

04:28.360 --> 04:29.050
Come now!

04:29.050 --> 04:30.540
Hurry! Hurry!

04:33.350 --> 04:35.780
You give that to me, Johan.

04:35.780 --> 04:37.670
Come away with us.

04:38.290 --> 04:39.800
You'll never...

04:39.800 --> 04:41.920
be one of them.

04:42.670 --> 04:45.130
Lieutenant! They're here!

04:57.970 --> 04:59.900
Thank you for coming!

04:59.900 --> 05:01.530
That was great!

05:01.910 --> 05:03.280
You were amazing!

05:03.280 --> 05:05.400
Heh, thanks.

05:05.780 --> 05:08.110
<i>Looks like Shima-kun's enjoying it, too.</i>

05:08.110 --> 05:09.800
Mitsumi, are you on break?

05:10.190 --> 05:12.160
Mika-chan! Good work!

05:12.160 --> 05:14.380
People really loved it.

05:14.930 --> 05:17.580
I hear it's the most popular 
first-year class attraction.

05:18.050 --> 05:20.450
So, isn't Nao-san coming 
to the school festival?

05:20.450 --> 05:22.730
She has a photo shoot all weekend.

05:22.730 --> 05:23.660
Oh...

05:23.660 --> 05:25.990
What's this? Did you two get even closer?

05:25.990 --> 05:28.590
Well, we follow each other 
on Pinsta and stuff.

05:28.590 --> 05:30.970
So that's why you...

05:29.570 --> 05:30.970
Mika!

05:30.970 --> 05:31.860
Yay!

05:31.860 --> 05:34.070
Wow! Yuna, Nocchi!

05:34.070 --> 05:35.950
Man, it's been ages!

05:35.950 --> 05:37.310
Told you we'd be here.

05:37.310 --> 05:39.410
That was so good!

05:39.410 --> 05:41.620
Aww, you guys! I'm so happy!

05:41.620 --> 05:42.730
Thanks!

05:43.150 --> 05:45.040
See you later, Mitsumi.

05:45.040 --> 05:45.740
Later.

05:45.740 --> 05:47.070
How's everyone doing?

05:47.070 --> 05:48.650
Just great!

05:48.650 --> 05:50.820
Nami really wanted to come, too.

05:50.820 --> 05:54.450
<b></b>Reception

05:51.180 --> 05:52.890
Come on, scoot in closer!

05:52.890 --> 05:54.450
Stop it. You're embarrassing me.

05:54.450 --> 05:55.990
When's your band playing?

05:55.990 --> 05:57.710
Oh, around three.

05:58.660 --> 06:02.290
<i>Oh, right. For them, Tokyo is home.</i>

06:13.220 --> 06:14.970
<b></b>Art Room

06:14.970 --> 06:16.980
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:14.970 --> 06:16.980
<b>Angel
Murashige Yuzuki
Class 1-3</b>

06:16.980 --> 06:18.170
What do you think?

06:18.170 --> 06:20.850
The way you use colors 
is really unique and amazing.

06:20.850 --> 06:23.610
What's this? This part's puffing out.

06:23.610 --> 06:24.870
You noticed?

06:24.870 --> 06:28.320
I used gesso to bring out 
Chiffon's fluffiness.

06:25.480 --> 06:28.320
<b>Chiffon = Yuzuki's Dog</b>

06:28.320 --> 06:30.270
You've got a keen eye, Mitsumi.

06:30.270 --> 06:33.580
Makoto just said "It's a masterpiece," 
and that was it.

06:33.580 --> 06:35.700
Oh, I haven't seen Makocchan all day.

06:35.700 --> 06:39.120
Right, she's showing around 
some friends from middle school.

06:39.120 --> 06:39.880
Oof!

06:39.880 --> 06:41.840
She said they'd come by the exhibit later.

06:41.840 --> 06:43.710
<i>I see. Even Makocchan...</i>

06:43.710 --> 06:45.000
W-Wow.

06:45.380 --> 06:48.280
This is really nice. Did you paint it?

06:48.280 --> 06:50.170
Thank you.

06:50.170 --> 06:54.010
I saw you in the hallway. 
So you're in the art club, huh?

06:54.010 --> 06:54.510
<b>throb</b>

06:54.010 --> 06:54.510
<b>throb</b>

06:54.010 --> 06:56.750
Murashige... What's your first name?

06:54.510 --> 06:55.010
<b>throb</b>

06:54.510 --> 06:55.010
<b>throb</b>

06:55.010 --> 06:55.510
<b>throb</b>

06:55.010 --> 06:55.510
<b>throb</b>

06:55.510 --> 06:56.010
<b>throb</b>

06:55.510 --> 06:56.010
<b>throb</b>

06:56.750 --> 06:58.520
<i>Wait, is he hitting on her?!</i>

06:59.550 --> 07:00.990
It's Yuzuki.

07:03.580 --> 07:06.340
You looked dead inside. Are you okay?

07:06.340 --> 07:07.390
Yeah...

07:07.390 --> 07:09.670
It's just, that's the fifth guy 
who's hit on me today.

07:09.670 --> 07:12.240
Fifth? You're so popular, Yuzu-chan.

07:12.240 --> 07:13.530
But, you know...

07:13.530 --> 07:17.290
I'm sick of people praising it 
without even looking at it.

07:17.610 --> 07:21.110
They pay no attention to something 
I poured my heart and soul into,

07:21.110 --> 07:23.670
then turn around and tell me 
they're interested in me?

07:24.600 --> 07:26.740
Is that supposed to make me happy?

07:27.840 --> 07:30.350
Oh, but don't tell anyone 
I said that. It's kinda mean.

07:30.350 --> 07:31.430
Got it!

07:31.830 --> 07:33.430
Excuse us.

07:34.260 --> 07:35.540
Hello!

07:36.300 --> 07:38.260
<i>I-I see.</i>

07:38.260 --> 07:43.270
<i>I've never gotten that kind of attention 
before, so I just think it's amazing.</i>

07:43.270 --> 07:46.660
Honestly, I wasn't having a good time 
with friends in middle school.

07:46.660 --> 07:50.650
I kept getting dragged 
into relationship drama.

07:51.120 --> 07:52.760
Take your time and look around.

07:52.760 --> 07:54.160
Thank you.

07:55.070 --> 07:57.660
<i>But everyone has their own issues.</i>

07:58.110 --> 08:01.210
I hear the home ec club's churros 
are good. Let's get some later.

08:01.210 --> 08:02.790
Sounds good! I'm in!

08:02.790 --> 08:03.730
You called?

08:05.410 --> 08:07.820
It's crazy. All the food stalls are swarmed.

08:07.820 --> 08:11.330
These looked like they'd sell out, 
so I bought yours as well.

08:11.330 --> 08:12.890
Your shift ends soon, right?

08:12.890 --> 08:14.900
Wow! Thanks!

08:14.900 --> 08:15.840
That'll be 200 yen.

08:15.840 --> 08:16.850
Okay!

08:15.840 --> 08:16.850
Thanks.

08:17.160 --> 08:20.390
I'll tell Mika that I got one for her, too.

08:20.390 --> 08:22.650
Oh, right. My friends from middle school.

08:22.650 --> 08:24.110
Mocchan and Sugita.

08:24.110 --> 08:25.100
Hi.

08:25.500 --> 08:26.860
I'm Murashige.

08:26.860 --> 08:28.100
I'm Iwakura.

08:28.100 --> 08:29.370
Hello.

08:29.370 --> 08:32.370
So how'd you become friends with Makoto?

08:32.370 --> 08:35.860
U-Uh... W-We were in the same class.

08:36.830 --> 08:38.370
Oh, okay.

08:38.370 --> 08:40.210
Well, have fun!

08:40.210 --> 08:41.620
Thanks.

08:41.620 --> 08:43.500
Sorry about all this.

08:43.500 --> 08:48.130
If you don't like people like me, 
don't force yourself to talk to me.

08:50.100 --> 08:50.880
Y...

08:50.880 --> 08:55.510
Yuzu reads the books I lend her and 
gives me her thoughts right away.

08:55.510 --> 08:59.590
A-Also, she painted that picture over there.

08:59.590 --> 09:02.660
She loves her dog with all her heart. 
Here it is sleeping.

09:02.660 --> 09:05.990
See the texture on his fur? 
She says it's to highlight his cuteness.

09:05.990 --> 09:08.280
Anyway, you can see 
the love she put into it.

09:08.960 --> 09:11.250
Hey, I've always wanted to ask.

09:11.250 --> 09:12.780
What breed is Chiffon, anyway?

09:17.040 --> 09:18.500
A Yorkshire Terrier.

09:20.280 --> 09:25.440
Man, I remembered how 
I was like that at first too.

09:25.440 --> 09:28.910
Yeah, you were. It feels 
like so long ago now.

09:29.270 --> 09:32.080
They're both good girls 
if you get to know them.

09:32.080 --> 09:33.470
I can tell.

09:33.470 --> 09:35.270
Oh, Mika-chan.

09:35.270 --> 09:37.050
I wanted to eat those churros!

09:37.430 --> 09:38.590
200 yen.

09:38.590 --> 09:39.550
Okay!

09:39.550 --> 09:41.930
Whoa, they look so good!

09:44.830 --> 09:47.580
It doesn't feel like it, 
but it's been half a year.

09:47.580 --> 09:49.380
Half a year already?

09:49.380 --> 09:50.370
Hmm?

09:50.370 --> 09:52.940
Okay, I'm off to help 
the literature club's table.

09:52.940 --> 09:55.200
And I have committee work.

09:55.200 --> 09:57.940
Aww, I wanted some more time to chill.

09:57.940 --> 09:59.200
Time for work.

09:59.200 --> 10:03.450
Oh, right. I heard the literature 
club's fanfic is super good.

10:03.450 --> 10:05.260
Much better response than we expected.

10:05.260 --> 10:07.430
We're considering printing more.

10:07.430 --> 10:10.080
Wow! Maybe I should read it too!

10:10.080 --> 10:11.460
Hey...

10:12.180 --> 10:15.440
We don't feel like it's only 
been six months, do we?

10:16.900 --> 10:17.920
See you.

10:22.090 --> 10:22.690
Bye.

10:22.690 --> 10:23.540
Later.

10:23.540 --> 10:24.360
See you.

10:29.510 --> 10:32.800
<i>We don't feel like it's only 
been six months, do we?</i>

10:38.020 --> 10:40.320
I'm back, Takamine-senpai.

10:40.320 --> 10:42.120
Welcome back, Mitsumi-san.

10:42.120 --> 10:48.000
<b>Stamp Rally
Prize Exchange</b>

10:42.690 --> 10:45.350
Looks like traffic's slowed down.

10:45.350 --> 10:48.000
And without incident. Lucky us.

10:49.390 --> 10:50.370
Excuse me!

10:51.140 --> 10:52.170
Hello.

10:52.170 --> 10:54.000
H-H-Hello!

10:54.000 --> 10:58.270
I asked the student council president 
for advice about exams this morning...

10:58.270 --> 10:59.510
Oh...

10:59.510 --> 11:04.070
He was so patient, and I feel 
a lot better after talking to him.

11:04.070 --> 11:04.970
Um...

11:04.970 --> 11:07.520
Please tell him I said thank you!

11:09.990 --> 11:12.020
Such a polite girl.

11:12.920 --> 11:14.520
But I get it.

11:14.520 --> 11:18.480
When you're feeling overwhelmed, 
a little kindness, well...

11:18.480 --> 11:20.780
It really picks you back up!

11:23.800 --> 11:25.410
Does it now?

11:27.470 --> 11:29.460
Huh? Holding down the fort?

11:29.460 --> 11:30.950
Wow, it's pretty dead now.

11:30.950 --> 11:34.250
You don't need to be such goody-two-shoes. 
One of you could take off.

11:35.170 --> 11:37.790
Ahem. Kazakami-san, the middle 
school girl from this morning...

11:37.790 --> 11:38.840
Hmm?

11:39.550 --> 11:40.470
Tomorrow?!

11:40.470 --> 11:42.840
<i>I've got the PM off. Let's hang out.</i>

11:42.840 --> 11:45.870
What's this? 
I'm usually the one who asks you.

11:45.870 --> 11:47.700
What do you wanna do? Aquarium?

11:47.700 --> 11:48.740
<i>Pass.</i>

11:48.740 --> 11:51.370
Oh, but this weekend's Sousuke's...

11:51.370 --> 11:52.020
Huh?

11:52.020 --> 11:54.980
Uh, I feel like he said he had plans?

11:54.980 --> 11:55.810
<b>Tsubame West High School</b>

11:55.770 --> 11:58.480
<b></b>Tsubame West High School
Festival

11:56.750 --> 11:58.480
Oho?

11:59.410 --> 12:01.300
"Plans," huh?

12:01.990 --> 12:05.990
<u>Scene 11: Hype and Excitement</u>

12:05.990 --> 12:08.490
<b>Tsubame West School Festival</b>

12:07.620 --> 12:08.490
Ahem.

12:08.490 --> 12:10.490
<b></b>

12:08.490 --> 12:11.500
Today is the second and final day.

12:11.500 --> 12:13.210
Let's stay on our toes

12:13.210 --> 12:16.130
and make sure everyone who attends 
enjoys the school festival!

12:16.510 --> 12:18.150
Yeah!

12:18.130 --> 12:20.880
<b>Tsubame West High School Festival</b>

12:18.150 --> 12:19.640
Good morning.

12:19.640 --> 12:21.520
Good morning!

12:22.110 --> 12:25.400
I heard Takizawa-senpai and 
Hayami-senpai started dating!

12:25.400 --> 12:26.850
Oh?

12:26.850 --> 12:27.910
Can I have one?

12:27.910 --> 12:28.680
Sure.

12:30.180 --> 12:32.860
I'm so jealous! I want some 
of that school festival magic!

12:32.860 --> 12:34.150
There, there.

12:34.150 --> 12:36.340
No news is good news, too.

12:36.900 --> 12:38.450
Thank you!

12:36.900 --> 12:40.400
<b>Class 1-3</b>

12:38.450 --> 12:40.400
Please watch your step as you leave.

12:40.400 --> 12:42.810
Apparently, we're killing it 
in the first-year vote!

12:42.810 --> 12:43.830
Seriously?

12:44.470 --> 12:46.780
I saw your performance, Shima-kun.

12:46.780 --> 12:50.020
You were great. You look like 
you're having plenty of fun!

12:50.020 --> 12:50.970
Uh, I guess?

12:50.970 --> 12:53.120
Aren't plays so much fun?

12:53.120 --> 12:57.090
The dance club is performing today, 
so you have time until the next show, right?

12:57.090 --> 12:58.070
Oh, uh, yes.

12:58.070 --> 13:00.760
Perfect! What incredible timing!

13:00.760 --> 13:02.860
The drama club will be 
performing soon, so Shima-kun—

13:02.860 --> 13:06.110
Oh? The churros are good? 
Maybe I'll go buy one.

13:06.110 --> 13:07.080
The line's really long.

13:07.080 --> 13:08.840
Better go now.

13:09.400 --> 13:13.770
You just have to come watch! Please!

13:11.280 --> 13:13.770
Um... what?

13:14.170 --> 13:16.400
I need to redeem myself after Charley Horse!

13:16.400 --> 13:19.150
You won't believe how much I've grown!

13:20.520 --> 13:21.820
Senpai...

13:22.650 --> 13:25.880
What's your endgame?

13:26.370 --> 13:27.830
I mean, a while back,

13:27.830 --> 13:31.020
you said that you wanted 
widespread acclaim...

13:34.160 --> 13:38.520
Oh, of course, I have big dreams! 
I want to be the best in the—

13:39.710 --> 13:42.550
But wait, what <i>is</i> my endgame?

13:42.550 --> 13:47.680
I'd like go as high as I can, but... 
that's more of a bonus or a sidenote.

13:47.680 --> 13:49.090
Hmm...

13:49.090 --> 13:50.930
So you don't know?

13:50.930 --> 13:56.230
I can't really imagine myself not 
being consumed by scriptwriting.

13:56.230 --> 13:59.310
So if I can make it my livelihood, 
that'd be amazing.

13:59.720 --> 14:05.190
Is there really an endpoint for daily 
routines like eating and going to work?

14:05.190 --> 14:07.380
I can't really picture it yet.

14:08.420 --> 14:14.670
Hm, hm, hm, hm... My little rose!

14:14.670 --> 14:16.170
The dance club performance is this way!

14:16.170 --> 14:17.790
Please come see it!

14:17.790 --> 14:19.760
Welcome.

14:19.760 --> 14:22.160
Kei-chan, do you want an egg sandwich?

14:22.160 --> 14:22.760
Yep!

14:22.760 --> 14:23.620
Here you are.

14:24.340 --> 14:27.300
Next is the first-year team's show.

14:27.300 --> 14:28.500
Welcome.

14:28.500 --> 14:31.970
One egg sandwich and 
one walnut bread, please.

14:44.230 --> 14:45.910
Thank you, come again.

14:45.910 --> 14:47.890
Okay, let's go eat over—

14:47.890 --> 14:48.890
Huh?

14:51.020 --> 14:52.110
Kei-chan?

14:52.610 --> 14:53.780
Keiri!

14:59.780 --> 15:01.030
Mama?

15:01.030 --> 15:02.550
Mama?!

15:06.280 --> 15:07.430
E'cuse me.

15:08.430 --> 15:10.910
Where is Class One-Tree?

15:11.260 --> 15:13.890
Do you know where your mom or dad is?

15:13.890 --> 15:16.570
Mama go to Class One-Tree too.

15:16.570 --> 15:18.290
What? Really?

15:18.290 --> 15:19.120
Yes.

15:19.580 --> 15:21.440
Class 3 is over there.

15:21.440 --> 15:22.940
<b>Class 1-3</b>

15:22.940 --> 15:24.570
How's it going?

15:24.570 --> 15:26.120
Oh, Iwakura-san.

15:26.120 --> 15:27.240
What's up?

15:27.240 --> 15:28.670
Excuse me.

15:29.730 --> 15:32.110
This boy says his mom is here.

15:32.110 --> 15:34.100
Wow, he's so cute!

15:34.100 --> 15:35.040
Hello.

15:35.040 --> 15:36.170
Did someone come by?

15:36.170 --> 15:38.850
We haven't opened up entry yet, so nope.

15:38.850 --> 15:39.450
Huh?

15:39.450 --> 15:41.670
Hoo boy. Not good.

15:41.670 --> 15:43.520
What's your name, little guy?

15:52.260 --> 15:54.240
I know that keychain.

15:54.240 --> 15:57.260
Are you Sh... Shima-kun's little brother?

15:58.740 --> 15:59.850
Wow!

16:00.280 --> 16:02.640
Yes. I'm Shima Keiri.

16:02.640 --> 16:04.100
I'm tree.

16:04.100 --> 16:05.460
Cute!

16:05.460 --> 16:07.180
Doesn't look much like him.

16:07.180 --> 16:09.360
I didn't know Shima-kun 
had such a tiny little brother!

16:09.360 --> 16:11.490
So what happened? Where's your mom—

16:13.740 --> 16:16.090
Uh... Keiri-kun, are you lost?

16:16.090 --> 16:19.330
Yes. But Mama is coming to Class One-Tree.

16:19.330 --> 16:20.250
Wait, wait, wait...

16:20.250 --> 16:22.940
What do we do?! His mom's 
gotta be looking for him!

16:22.940 --> 16:24.410
We might've missed the PA!

16:24.410 --> 16:26.900
I'll run to HQ and see if she's there!

16:26.900 --> 16:27.570
Where's Shima?

16:27.570 --> 16:29.550
Watching the drama club! I'll go get him!

16:29.550 --> 16:32.420
Keiri-kun, can you sit here and wait?

16:32.420 --> 16:33.180
Yes.

16:33.180 --> 16:35.000
I like your backpack.

16:35.000 --> 16:35.840
Cool, right?

16:35.840 --> 16:36.690
Let me check it out.

16:36.330 --> 16:38.190
<i>He's got nerves of steel!</i>

16:36.690 --> 16:38.180
Okay.

16:41.810 --> 16:45.310
<b>Drama Club School Festival Performance</b>

16:41.810 --> 16:45.310
<b>K's Sunday</b>

16:42.260 --> 16:44.530
Sorry, but I'm coming in.

16:44.530 --> 16:46.720
What are you doing here?!

16:46.720 --> 16:48.060
Wh-Who is this?

16:48.060 --> 16:49.770
A debt collector.

16:49.770 --> 16:50.820
What do you want?

16:50.820 --> 16:52.880
The payment isn't due yet! H-Hey!

16:52.880 --> 16:56.200
Talk about gloomy. 
Why don't you open a window?

16:56.990 --> 16:58.700
Where's your father?

16:58.700 --> 17:00.280
He isn't here.

17:00.280 --> 17:03.830
Nothing good'll come out of hiding him.

17:04.280 --> 17:06.070
Heh. You get it, don't you?

17:06.070 --> 17:09.230
You're the outsider here.

17:09.230 --> 17:12.220
Mamoru, let's go! I'll get the money!

17:13.030 --> 17:14.910
What a waste of time.

17:14.910 --> 17:17.840
Some Sunday this turned out to be.

17:24.480 --> 17:26.570
Thank you very much!

17:27.730 --> 17:30.230
Th-Thank you very much.

17:32.190 --> 17:33.360
Kanechika!

17:33.360 --> 17:34.310
Hey.

17:34.310 --> 17:36.060
That was amazing, man!

17:36.060 --> 17:37.310
R-Really?

17:37.310 --> 17:38.950
No, like, for real!

17:38.950 --> 17:42.730
Honestly, your original stuff 
flies way over my head, but this?

17:42.730 --> 17:45.680
It was crazy how you foreshadowed 
the entire second half!

17:45.680 --> 17:47.530
Anyway, seriously, it was awesome!

17:48.100 --> 17:51.650
Really? Of course it was!

17:51.650 --> 17:56.890
I thought everyone was going 
to love this one for sure!

17:56.890 --> 17:58.680
Thanks for coming to see it!

17:58.680 --> 17:59.760
Sure!

18:02.010 --> 18:03.060
Oh! Shima-kun...

18:03.060 --> 18:03.970
Sousuke!

18:03.970 --> 18:05.670
What's up, Mukai?

18:05.670 --> 18:08.660
Your little brother got lost 
and came to our class.

18:08.660 --> 18:09.350
Huh?

18:09.350 --> 18:11.610
What do you mean? What's happening?

18:11.610 --> 18:13.100
You mean my mom's here, too?

18:13.100 --> 18:14.230
Shima-kun...

18:13.100 --> 18:14.230
That'd be my guess.

18:14.230 --> 18:15.930
What?!

18:18.480 --> 18:20.290
He came to our class alone?

18:20.290 --> 18:23.290
Yeah, shocking. He's only three, right?

18:23.290 --> 18:25.290
The kid's a trooper. Hasn't cried once.

18:25.760 --> 18:29.220
That's weird. He's usually so timid.

18:29.220 --> 18:31.920
Timid? That chatterbox?

18:31.920 --> 18:33.860
Wait, I get it.

18:33.860 --> 18:34.920
What?

18:35.310 --> 18:39.430
Kids can tell when you 
don't want them around.

18:41.020 --> 18:45.160
Look, I just don't know how 
to deal with little kids.

18:45.620 --> 18:50.270
I'm his stepbrother. If I showered him 
with affection, Dad'd feel awkward.

18:50.270 --> 18:53.930
I used cram school as an excuse 
to get away from home in middle school.

18:54.620 --> 18:57.940
I don't think Keiri's all that 
interested in me, either.

18:58.420 --> 19:01.200
I'm not an expert on 
your family or anything...

19:01.200 --> 19:05.490
But you seriously think a three-year-old kid 
wouldn't care about his big bro?

19:05.490 --> 19:07.890
You come up with the weirdest excuses, man.

19:07.890 --> 19:10.130
Oh, I need to call Mom.

19:10.130 --> 19:11.960
She's gotta be freaking out.

19:13.170 --> 19:15.690
<i>Why did Mom come today?</i>

19:16.210 --> 19:19.840
<b>Mom</b>

19:16.570 --> 19:19.840
<i>I guess she's going to see the class play.</i>

19:21.450 --> 19:22.820
<i>But why?</i>

19:24.150 --> 19:26.460
What, really? The classroom?

19:26.850 --> 19:28.590
All right. I'll be right there.

19:28.590 --> 19:30.200
Thanks, Sousuke.

19:30.730 --> 19:35.000
Sorry, it seems he went 
to his brother's classroom.

19:35.000 --> 19:37.310
Oh, good. You must be so relieved.

19:37.310 --> 19:39.800
I'll go right there and pick him up.

19:41.690 --> 19:46.220
Ah! Are you Shima... Sousuke-kun's mother?

19:46.220 --> 19:47.290
Y-Yes.

19:47.290 --> 19:48.790
Oh, good!

19:48.790 --> 19:53.800
I'm Shima... Sousuke-kun's 
classmate, Iwakura!

19:53.800 --> 19:56.720
Uh... Keiri-kun's in our classroom!

19:56.720 --> 19:59.300
Oh, Sousuke just told me over the phone.

19:59.300 --> 20:01.810
Oh, thank g...

20:02.540 --> 20:04.300
Are you okay?

20:04.300 --> 20:06.500
Let's head there, slow and steady.

20:09.100 --> 20:09.680
Oh.

20:09.680 --> 20:11.070
There he is.

20:14.770 --> 20:17.190
He's laughing his butt off.

20:17.190 --> 20:20.130
Look, Keiri-kun. It's your brother.

20:20.130 --> 20:21.070
Good for you!

20:38.230 --> 20:42.200
Bro...

20:42.640 --> 20:44.650
Bro...

20:45.890 --> 20:48.480
He must be relieved to see his big bro.

20:48.480 --> 20:51.210
Yeah, you two are brothers, all right.

20:51.210 --> 20:52.640
Huh? How do you mean?

20:52.640 --> 20:54.350
You're both too considerate.

20:54.350 --> 20:56.150
For better or worse.

20:57.330 --> 20:59.930
<i>Was he... being considerate of me?</i>

20:59.320 --> 21:03.360
<b>\hRuns away when they cross paths\h</b>

21:00.610 --> 21:01.860
I'm home.

21:02.940 --> 21:07.370
<b>\h\h\h\h\hStares at him from afar\h\h\h\h\h</b>

21:04.530 --> 21:06.460
Stare.

21:07.850 --> 21:10.660
<i>Wait, I think I was like that 
growing up, too...</i>

21:23.990 --> 21:24.750
Sh...

21:25.180 --> 21:27.450
Shall we wait for Mom in the hallway?

21:28.700 --> 21:29.740
Yep.

21:36.290 --> 21:38.920
Sorry for the trouble. 
I should have paid more attention.

21:38.920 --> 21:40.940
No, not at all.

21:41.420 --> 21:43.100
<i>Shima-kun's mom...</i>

21:43.100 --> 21:46.990
The girl earlier was so thoughtful, too.

21:44.820 --> 21:46.990
<i>She seems like a really nice person.</i>

21:46.990 --> 21:50.200
This really is a fine school.

21:56.160 --> 21:58.370
Our class is down this hallway.

22:10.010 --> 22:10.010


22:27.450 --> 22:31.710
<i>A gentle breeze, the setting sun</i>

22:31.710 --> 22:36.030
<i>Today was another good day</i>

22:36.030 --> 22:40.370
<i>Forgetting all the plans I made</i>

22:40.370 --> 22:44.380
<i>I'll walk to the next station over</i>

22:44.380 --> 22:49.050
<i>The more I trip and fall</i>

22:49.050 --> 22:53.060
<i>The better I get at picking myself back up</i>

22:53.060 --> 22:57.630
<i>Through honest dialogue and heart-to-hearts</i>

22:57.630 --> 23:02.030
<i>The warmth seeps into my soul</i>

23:02.030 --> 23:06.320
<i>Humming as I take the roundabout way</i>

23:06.320 --> 23:10.450
<i>My world is an unsolved mystery</i>

23:10.450 --> 23:14.960
<i>Top speed, toes and heels, strides</i>

23:14.960 --> 23:19.120
<i>Each one of us walks differently</i>

23:19.120 --> 23:23.640
<i>All the same, we wave goodbye to dusk</i>

23:23.640 --> 23:27.630
<i>As a new morning dawns</i>

23:27.630 --> 23:32.300
<i>Wanting to protect this everyday life</i>

23:32.300 --> 23:35.520
<i>With a hop, jump, and skip</i>

23:35.520 --> 23:38.770
<i>See you tomorrow</i>
